From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:03:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 34/44] client: no fall damage landing in water, as in
 Minecraft

A fall onto the bottom of shallow water hurt as on land, less what the
water braked: 20 m into water 2 deep took 11 HP. Minecraft ends the fall
in water. Now a landing while any part of the box is in a node of the
group water does no damage.

Checked in the native build, a fall of 20 m: on land 14 HP, into water
1 or 2 deep none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/client/clientenvironment.cpp b/src/client/clientenvironment.cpp
index 3387fc5d1..c7c50b286 100644
--- a/src/client/clientenvironment.cpp
+++ b/src/client/clientenvironment.cpp
@@ -178,6 +178,10 @@ void ClientEnvironment::step(float dtime)
 		*/
 
 		lplayer->move(dtime_part, this, &player_collisions);
+
+		// As in Minecraft, water ends a fall: landing in it does no damage
+		if (lplayer->water_depth > 0.0f)
+			player_collisions.clear();
 	}
 
 	bool player_immortal = false;
